  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "iEaMdkRe9o1LrVKzOJd6Z7v1dis=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:09.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## One provisioned agent per product\n\nVetra Studio is the browser UI for the **Vetra agent**. Each studio you create is a *dedicated cloud agent* tied to your identity, running in an isolated environment that hosts the agent, its workspace and the preview services, on its own `<slug>.vetra.io` subdomain. Opening it lands you inside Powerhouse Connect at `<slug>.vetra.io/d/<drive-id>` \u2014 the Studio is not a separate app but a chat pane bolted onto Connect, with the phase-cycle cards, documents and build preview in the main pane.\n\nAccess is gated: log in at vetra.io with a wallet via Renown, open the Products dashboard at `/user`, and either paste an invite code, join the waitlist, or run it locally. With a code, the Anthropic API key powering the agent is supplied behind the code, so there is nothing to enter. Products move `Provisioning\u2026 \u2192 Ready` before they can be opened. The product is **pre-alpha** \u2014 back documents up by download or GitHub at the end of a cycle.\n\n## The four phases\n\n| Phase | What happens |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 Ideate | Frame problem and audience \u2014 problem, audience and brand sheets, a feature, a work breakdown structure |\n| 2 Specify | Pin down data model, workflow and states \u2014 document models grouped into projects |\n| 3 Build | The agent generates and tests code, with a live preview of the running app |\n| 4 Deploy | Publish the package and run it in Vetra Cloud environments |\n\nAvailability is progress-gated: BUILD shows a preview only after the agent scaffolds a reactor project, and DEPLOY requires a Renown sign-in.\n\nChat sessions are **CRDT documents stored in the studio's reactor**, so they survive restarts, are shareable by URL (`?session=<id>`), and are scoped per identity \u2014 clicking **Authorize agent** switches the studio from a generated `did:key` to your wallet `did:pkh` and therefore changes which sessions the list shows. Agent tool calls stream inline as expandable cards (`spec-create`, `spec-generate`, `reactor-project-init`, `spec-preview-show`, plus workspace Read/Write/Edit).\n\nNote a naming tension in the docs: the Build section describes \"Vetra Studio\" as the local `ph vetra` builder environment, while GetStarted describes this hosted agent product. Both names are in use.\n\n_Source: `apps/academy/docs/academy/01-GetStarted/00-VetraStudio.md`, Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:36:09.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:36:09.000Z"
    }
  },
